## 8. Documentation Discipline

### 8.1 Vault First

For Hermes fleet and infrastructure work, read the Obsidian vault first when relevant.

Canonical root map:

```text
Vault Root Structure.md
```

Global front doors:

```text
Home.md
Index.md
README.md
```

Hermes Ops front doors commonly include:

```text
Operational/Hermes Ops/README.md
Operational/Hermes Ops/Hermes Fleet Master Index.md
Operational/Hermes Ops/Hermes Atlas Board.md
```

### 8.2 Documentation Bundles

For infrastructure changes, produce or update:

1. Step-by-step operational note.
2. One-page checklist.
3. Simple diagram.
4. Cross-links among related notes.
5. Front-door references where appropriate.

### 8.3 Drift Handling

When docs disagree:

1. Identify the canonical source.
2. Compare live runtime state.
3. Update stale notes or mirrors.
4. Re-open changed files.
5. Run available consistency checks.
6. Report what was aligned and what remains unconfirmed.

Do not update only a deep note while front-door pages remain stale.

